Graft string.pack / string.unpack / string.packsize into 5.2.1.

Factorio's Lua is 5.2.1 with these three backported from 5.4.6. Stock 5.2.1 has
no such thing, so without this the oracle is missing a feature the real sandbox
has -- and `--persist=packed` is built entirely on it.

The implementation lives in strpack.c, copied into src/ by fetch.sh, so it can
be read and diffed against upstream instead of living inside a patch hunk. It is
#included rather than compiled separately because it uses lstrlib.c's already
included lua.h/lauxlib.h and needs no separate translation unit.

Semantics follow the in-game probe, not upstream 5.4: with no integer subtype an
integer option truncates its argument rather than raising. See the header comment
in strpack.c and the table in agents/sandbox.md.

--- a/src/lstrlib.c
+++ b/src/lstrlib.c
@@ -928,6 +928,15 @@
 }
 
 /* }====================================================== */
+
+
+/*
+** {======================================================
+** PACK/UNPACK, backported from Lua 5.4.6. The implementation is an ordinary
+** file so it can be diffed against upstream; see strpack.c.
+** =======================================================
+*/
+#include "strpack.c"
 
 
 static const luaL_Reg strlib[] = {
@@ -945,6 +954,9 @@
   {"reverse", str_reverse},
   {"sub", str_sub},
   {"upper", str_upper},
+  {"pack", fk_str_pack},
+  {"packsize", fk_str_packsize},
+  {"unpack", fk_str_unpack},
   {NULL, NULL}
 };
 
